def defect_rotor_frequency_reads_as_k4_on_front() -> dict:
    """[DERIVED-A (part i: the restriction/chain-rule identity) + FRAMING (parts ii-iii:
    two NAMED residues, not silently folded in)] — WP-MASS-MEASURE keystone bridge:
    how the DEFECT's meta-time rotor frequency ω (R-007, §A.4 'mass = ω') reads as the
    front wavenumber k_4 that R-017's Klein-Gordon reduction (§B.2.1) consumes as rest
    mass. (2026-07-02)

    THE GAP THIS MAKES EXACT / NAMES. R-017's k_4 is the e_4-Fourier label of a
    fluctuation linearized around the CANTED VACUUM (§D.4.6 — 'not around a defect');
    R-007's ω is the DEFECT's meta-time rotor frequency in τ_5. Until now the
    identification 'm = k_4' lived in the corpus only as a docstring string
    (Cl41Wave.klein_gordon) plus one paper cross-cite (§B.2.1 → §A.4). This primitive
    banks the derivable core exactly and NAMES the two residues that remain open. Per
    the Phase F lesson (ledger N-LEPTON-EPS-FROM-L-ORBIT: a tuned special configuration
    hid a mismatch), the identity is checked on GENERIC, non-special configurations —
    including a conjugated rotor axis and the central E.

    (i) DERIVED-A — the restriction identity. A meta-time rotor
            q_h(τ_5) = cos(ω τ_5 / 2) + û sin(ω τ_5 / 2),   û simple, û² = −1,
        restricted to the banked wavefront lock x_4 = c_meta · τ_5 (§A.4), IS the
        x_4-profile
            q_h(x_4 / c_meta) = cos(k_4 x_4 / 2) + û sin(k_4 x_4 / 2),
            k_4 = ω / c_meta.
        Chain rule — exact, and AXIS-INDEPENDENT: any û with û² = −1, including the
        central E = I_4·e_5. Engine-checked below at generic ω, c_meta, five sample
        points, and three independent axes (e_12; a conjugated generic axis R e_13 R̃;
        the central E). In natural units (c_meta = 1, the Opening's convention)
        k_4 = ω = m: the defect's rotor frequency and its front-restricted wavenumber
        are ONE number. Rotor-level x_4-period is 4π/k_4 with the half-angle sign flip
        at 2π/k_4 (spinor inheritance, §A.4); the wavenumber extracted numerically from
        the rotor's phase advance along x_4 equals ω/c_meta.

    (ii) FRAMING residue — the one-particle-sector claim. Part (i) shows the defect's
        rotor history, READ along the front (x_4 = c_meta·τ_5), is x_4-periodic at
        k_4 = ω/c_meta. That the vacuum-linearized fluctuation field of a defect-bearing
        region has its one-particle sector AT this k_4 — i.e. that R-017's Fourier label
        numerically equals the defect's ω — is the physical identification the paper
        asserts at §B.2.1 by cross-cite to R-007. NOT derived here; named open (Paper-2
        soliton-fluctuation spectrum question, §D.4.6).

    (iii) FRAMING residue — the complex-unit hand-off. The rotor axis û is
        meta-time/central content (the ℍ factor, or E = I_4·e_5); the KG reduction's
        i is the transverse defect-selected B_a (§B.3.1 centralizer). The restriction
        identity (i) holds for ANY simple û — it does not depend on resolving this —
        but WHICH unit carries the k_4 phase in the observer's complex structure is
        the §B.3.1 orientation mechanism, whose derivation AS a hand-off (E → B_a) is
        owed. Named open, not blurred. [RESOLVED 2026-07-02 — R-127
        front_phase_handoff_selects_winding_axis, and NOT via the named hand-off
        route: no E→B_a conversion exists; the observer-visible mass phase never
        leaves the winding blade (leptons û = ±B_a; quark sector û = ±I_4·B_q per
        R-128). Sweep annotation.]

    CONSEQUENCES (worklist WP-MASS-MEASURE, the five signature chains): chain (2)
    dispersion E² = p² + m² becomes implied-by-banked MODULO residue (ii) alone
    (R-017 + this primitive); chain (5) oscillation inherits the beat-phase FORM
    (two superposed rotor frequencies on the linear face beat at Δm² = ω_i² − ω_j²)
    conditional on (ii) plus the UNDERIVED mixing (PMNS defused,
    `pmns_no_substrate_derivation`); chain (1) cyclotron inherits its inertia leg
    conditional on (ii) plus the charged-defect worldline EOM [UPDATE 2026-07-02:
    that EOM is now BANKED — charged_defect_worldline_eom_cyclotron, R-124 — so
    chain (1) sits MODULO residue (ii) alone, like chain (2)]. Chains (3)
    gravitational coupling (already banked via R-037/R-038 +
    `equivalence_principle_protection`) and (4) decay-energy residual (genuinely
    #1-gap-gated) are unaffected.

    WOULD CHANGE IF (the residues close): (ii) closes if the linearized fluctuation
    spectrum around a defect-bearing configuration is computed and its one-particle
    pole sits at k_4 = ω/c_meta; (iii) closes if the §B.3.1 orientation mechanism is
    extended to an explicit E → B_a phase hand-off on the front.
    """
    # generic, non-special parameters (Phase F discipline: nothing tuned to a target)
    omega = 0.937
    c_meta = 1.31
    k4 = omega / c_meta
    ONE = SCALAR

    # three independent axes û with û² = −1
    ang = 0.4135
    R = MV.from_dict({(): math.cos(ang), (2, 3): math.sin(ang)})
    Rt = MV.from_dict({(): math.cos(ang), (2, 3): -math.sin(ang)})
    axes = {
        "e12 (L-orbit simple bivector)": e(1, 2),
        "R e13 R~ (generic conjugated axis)": R * e(1, 3) * Rt,
        "E = I4*e5 (central, Cl(4,1))": e(1, 2, 3, 4, 5),
    }

    def _rotor(u, angle_full):
        """q = cos(angle/2) + u sin(angle/2) for a simple u with u² = −1."""
        return MV.from_dict({(): math.cos(angle_full / 2.0)}) + math.sin(angle_full / 2.0) * u

    def _mv_norm(x):
        return sum(abs(c) for _, c in x.terms)

    per_axis = {}
    for name, u in axes.items():
        u_sq_is_minus_one = _mv_norm(u * u + ONE) < 1e-12
        # restriction identity at five generic sample points
        max_diff = 0.0
        for tau5 in (0.0, 0.377, 1.234, 2.9, 5.01):
            x4 = c_meta * tau5
            q_tau = _rotor(u, omega * tau5)
            q_x4 = _rotor(u, k4 * x4)
            max_diff = max(max_diff, _mv_norm(q_tau + (-1.0) * q_x4))
        # extract the wavenumber numerically from the phase advance along x_4:
        # q ∈ span{1, u}; with u² = −1, q·u = −b + a·u so b = −⟨q u⟩_0, a = ⟨q⟩_0.
        def _theta_at(x4_val, u=u):
            q = _rotor(u, k4 * x4_val)
            a = q.coeff(())
            b = -(q * u).coeff(())
            return 2.0 * math.atan2(b, a)
        x4_ref, h = 0.6, 1e-6
        k4_extracted = (_theta_at(x4_ref + h) - _theta_at(x4_ref)) / h
        per_axis[name] = {
            "u_squared_is_minus_one": u_sq_is_minus_one,
            "max_restriction_diff": max_diff,
            "k4_extracted": k4_extracted,
        }

    restriction_identity_exact = all(
        v["u_squared_is_minus_one"] and v["max_restriction_diff"] < 1e-12
        for v in per_axis.values()
    )
    k4_extraction_matches = all(
        abs(v["k4_extracted"] - k4) < 1e-5 for v in per_axis.values()
    )

    # rotor-level periodicity on the front: sign flip at x_4 = 2π/k_4, return at 4π/k_4
    u = axes["R e13 R~ (generic conjugated axis)"]
    q_at_half = _rotor(u, k4 * (2.0 * math.pi / k4))       # angle 2π → q = −1
    q_at_full = _rotor(u, k4 * (4.0 * math.pi / k4))       # angle 4π → q = +1
    half_angle_sign_flip = _mv_norm(q_at_half + ONE) < 1e-9
    full_period_4pi_over_k4 = _mv_norm(q_at_full + (-1.0) * ONE) < 1e-9

    # natural-units reading: with c_meta = 1, k_4 = ω = m literally
    natural_units_k4_equals_omega = abs((omega / 1.0) - omega) < 1e-15

    assert restriction_identity_exact, "restriction identity q(τ5)|lock = q(x4/c) must be exact on all axes"
    assert k4_extraction_matches, "extracted front wavenumber must equal ω/c_meta on all axes"
    assert half_angle_sign_flip and full_period_4pi_over_k4, "half-angle periodicity on the front failed"
    assert natural_units_k4_equals_omega

    return {
        "outcome": "BANKED — DERIVED-A restriction identity + two NAMED FRAMING residues",
        "tier": ("DERIVED-A (part i restriction identity, axis-independent, generic-config "
                 "checked) + FRAMING (part ii one-particle-sector-at-k4; part iii E→B_a "
                 "complex-unit hand-off). The identification R-017 consumes is (i) ∧ (ii); "
                 "only (i) is derived here."),
        "worklist_ref": "WP-MASS-MEASURE (keystone bridge; chains 1/2/5 inherit)",
        "k4_over_omega_expected": 1.0 / c_meta,
        "per_axis_checks": per_axis,
        "restriction_identity_exact": restriction_identity_exact,
        "k4_extraction_matches": k4_extraction_matches,
        "half_angle_sign_flip_at_2pi_over_k4": half_angle_sign_flip,
        "rotor_period_4pi_over_k4": full_period_4pi_over_k4,
        "natural_units_k4_equals_omega": natural_units_k4_equals_omega,
        "framing_residue_ii_one_particle_sector": (
            "that the vacuum-linearized fluctuation one-particle sector of a defect-bearing "
            "region sits AT k_4 = ω/c_meta is asserted at §B.2.1 via cross-cite to R-007; "
            "NOT derived here — Paper-2 soliton-fluctuation spectrum question (§D.4.6)."
        ),
        "framing_residue_iii_complex_unit_handoff": (
            "the rotor axis û is central/meta-time content (ℍ or E = I_4·e_5); the KG "
            "reduction's i is the transverse defect-selected B_a (§B.3.1). The identity (i) "
            "is axis-independent so it does not resolve WHICH unit carries the k_4 phase; "
            "the E → B_a hand-off derivation is owed."
        ),
        "would_change_if": (
            "(ii) closes: linearized fluctuation spectrum around a defect-bearing "
            "configuration computed, one-particle pole at k_4 = ω/c_meta; (iii) closes: "
            "§B.3.1 orientation mechanism extended to an explicit E → B_a hand-off."
        ),
    }


